# Normalise text files to LF in the index and on checkout, on every platform
# (#931). Every tracked text file here was already LF, but nothing enforced it,
# and during #928 a single pathlib.write_text() from a Windows checkout rewrote
# tests/test_validator_harness.py to CRLF -- 676 of 806 changed lines in that
# commit were pure line-ending churn around ~134 lines of real change. Churn
# like that hides the actual diff from review, defeats git blame, and invites
# normalisation scripts that damage string literals containing \r\n.
#
# "text=auto" leaves git to detect which files are text (binaries are left
# alone); "eol=lf" fixes the working-tree ending so a Windows checkout cannot
# reintroduce CRLF through an editor or a script's default newline.
* text=auto eol=lf
